<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vasily Yaroslavich of Serpukhov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1483</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vasily Yaroslavich was prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serpukhov">Serpukhov</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borovsk">Borovsk</a>, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-the-bold">Vladimir the Bold</a> and brother-in-law of Grand Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasily-ii-of-moscow">Vasily II of Moscow</a>. During <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>'s dynastic civil war he loyally supported Vasily II against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-shemyaka">Dmitry Shemyaka</a>. In 1456 the grand prince nevertheless had him arrested and annexed Serpukhov, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a>. He spent the rest of his life in prison and died in 1483.</p></div>
